  "term": "paraphrenia",
  "definition": "Paraphrenia is a long-lasting psychotic disorder marked mainly by strong delusions while thinking and overall personality remain relatively preserved. It is linked with paranoia and paranoid dementia, with less personality decline than schizophrenia and not matching the full picture of delusional disorder.",
